Logging to Host via JTAG
By default, the logging library uses the vprintf-like function to write formatted output
to the dedicated UART. By calling a simple API, all log output may be routed to JTAG instead, making logging
several times faster. For details, please refer to Section Logging to Host.
Thread Safety
The log string is first written into a memory buffer and then sent to the UART for printing. Log
calls are thread-safe, i.e., logs of different threads do not conflict with each other.
